A parser splits a pipe separated row without escaping the delimiter and reports what it got.
String line = "12|7|20";
String[] p = line.split("|");
System.out.println(p.length + ":" + (p.length > 0 ? p[0] : "none"));
What does the console show?

A roster written on a system that ends lines with two characters crashes on its first data row, whose numeric field is the three characters 9, 1 and a carriage return.
String[] p = line.split(",");
int score = Integer.parseInt(p[1]);
Which statement identifies the fault?

A roster row arrives as "mia,91" followed by a carriage return, and the score must parse. Fill the blank so the reader works on a file written that way.
for (String line : lines) {
  String[] cells = line.split(",");
  int score = Integer.parseInt(_____)  ;
  total += score;
}

A padded roster row is parsed and printed with this fragment.
String line = "  mia , 91 ";
String[] padded = line.split(",");
System.out.println("[" + padded[0].trim() + "][" + padded[1].trim() + "]");
What does the console show?

A badge file stores a colour code in hex, and the row "lamp,1A" must yield its decimal value. This line does the conversion.
int v = Integer.parseInt(p[1], 16);
What integer does v hold?

A reader cuts each row at its first comma and needs the numeric field from what follows. Fill the blank.
int cut = line.indexOf(',');
String name = line.substring(0, cut);
String value = line.substring(____).trim();

A log row is "site:glen, north:12", where the site text itself contains a colon, and the reader must take everything before the final colon.
String cut = line.lastIndexOf(':');
String place = line.substring(0, cut);
System.out.println(place);
What does the console show?

A reader must skip the header without knowing its text, and the first row is "site,cm". Fill the blank so the header is recognised by what it cannot supply.
String row = sc.nextLine();
String[] cols = row.split(",");
if (cols.length == 2 && !isNumeric(cols[1])) { /* header */ } else { /* data */ }
Which helper makes the header branch true?

A reader counts the data rows in this buffer while skipping blanks.
String data = "site,cm\nnorth,6\n\nsouth,9\n";
Scanner sc = new Scanner(data);
sc.nextLine();
int n = 0;
while (sc.hasNextLine()) { if (!sc.nextLine().isBlank()) n++; }
System.out.println(n);
What integer is printed?

A counter should report 2 for the buffer "site,cm" then "west,4" then a blank line then "east,8", but it reports 1.
String data = "site,cm\nwest,4\n\neast,8\n";
Scanner input = new Scanner(data);
input.nextLine();
int n = 0;
while (input.hasNextLine()) {
  String row = input.nextLine();
  if (!row.isBlank()) continue;
  n++;
}
Which statement identifies the fault?

A reader must keep going after a corrupt row, but it stops at the first one. The file holds site,cm then north,6 then bad,x then south,9, and the code is
int total = 0;
try {
  while (scan.hasNextLine()) {
    String[] row = scan.nextLine().split(",");
    total += Integer.parseInt(row[1]);
  }
} catch (NumberFormatException e) { }
Which statement identifies the fault?

A reader counts only the rows it managed to parse, and the file holds north,6 then bad,x then south,9. Fill the blank so the tally is 2.
int n = 0;
while (feed.hasNextLine()) {
  String[] cells = feed.nextLine().split(",");
  try {
    int depth = Integer.parseInt(cells[1]);
    /* blank */
  } catch (NumberFormatException bad) { }
}

A doubled comma leaves an empty middle field, and the reader reports what happens.
String line = "west,,9";
String[] fields = line.split(",");
System.out.println(fields.length + ":" + Integer.parseInt(fields[1]));
What does the console show?

A census adds 50,000 households, each holding 50,000 people, into a single int accumulator.
int total = 0;
for (int h = 0; h < 50000; h++) { total += 50000 * 50000; }
What integer does total hold when the loop finishes?

A census program reports a negative population for 50,000 households of 50,000 people each.
int households = 50000;
int total = 0;
for (int h = 0; h < households; h++) { total += households * 50000; }
Which statement identifies the fault?

A till adds ten ten-cent coins into a double and prints the total to two decimal places.
double total = 0.0;
for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) { total += 0.10; }
System.out.printf("%.2f%n", total);
What does the console show?

A report must print the mean of the passing scores 90, 80 and 30 with a pass mark of 70, but it prints 66.
int sum = 0, kept = 0, rows = 0;
while (marks.hasNextLine()) {
  String[] cols = marks.nextLine().split(",");
  rows++;
  int mark = Integer.parseInt(cols[1]);
  if (mark >= 70) { sum += mark; kept++; }
}
System.out.println(sum / rows);
Which statement identifies the fault?

A report writes the qualifying rows to a file first, then averages the file. The rows it kept are the strings deep,14 and mid,11, and it finishes with
int sum = 0, n = 0;
for (String row : kept) { sum += Integer.parseInt(row.split(",")[1]); n++; }
System.out.println(sum / n);
What does the console show?

A report must print the shallowest reading that is at least 10 cm, and the rows are 6, 14, 11 and 9.
int best = 0;
while (gauge.hasNextLine()) {
  String[] reading = gauge.nextLine().split(",");
  int v = Integer.parseInt(reading[1]);
  if (v > best) best = v;
}
System.out.println(best);
What does the console show?

A report must write each row's fields separated by a semicolon instead of the comma it read. Fill the blank.
out.println(_____);
A keeps both fields, trims their padding and joins them with a semicolon.
